00b-e5e9-541c-8388-24405da1e57d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379782} {:answer/id #uuid "3bde1763-c17f-5905-bbb1-e2a6e02b57e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379783} {:answer/id #uuid "ea2a1b06-67db-5221-afa2-7618ffd9d26d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379784}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcb1bef2-5cce-573a-bf79-bbfbc33b724f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379781} :answer-field/id #uuid "0352c60c-3be5-56be-b959-d8ac481c11cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379779}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8166eb05-ff92-507f-8eb2-6ecb8cda44b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-35866" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are neither open nor closed?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le x<2,\\,0<y<2}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}<2,}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2},\\,-1\\le x\\le 1}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *neither open nor closed*. It contains some of its boundary points, for example, the point $(0,1).$ On the other hand, it does not contain some other boundary points, for example, the point $(1,0).$\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186193325 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f3149834-ef92-5016-a84a-40b207fee519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets of Real Numbers" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048439 :topic/math-academy-id 4097 :topic/title "Open and Closed Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "facf23d5-9117-50d0-ada3-7655fa8f7201" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191878} {:answer/id #uuid "2e69bb7e-e939-5070-bb59-8f9d1092af92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191879} {:answer/id #uuid "434a1c4a-a3e9-5ea0-b8d0-a0659339a9b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191880} {:answer/id #uuid "5bb4d92c-87f1-5feb-a1b6-07dcd9ccb1bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191881} {:answer/id #uuid "645d283a-9751-5b8d-bf9f-045f81ec8255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191882}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3b69c7f3-c351-59ac-bb07-0af3d7e41c2c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186191877}] :question/id #uuid "48c2f172-a7b8-52c3-85b9-54d5dd4bd677" :question/math-academy-id "q-36443" :question/prob